{"path":"js/packages/host-companion/README.md","ref":"600ca4ec1f763b6662f205fe8cb068bba809c1c1","side":"new","lines":[{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":1,"text":"# VitaDeck Host Companion"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":2,"text":""},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":3,"text":"The Host Companion runs on a Mac, Windows or Linux computer near your Vita. A Deck App sends it **Host Control** commands over the LAN, and the companion runs them on the computer. It needs Node.js 24."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":4,"text":""},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":5,"text":"```sh"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":6,"text":"npm install -g @vitadeck/host-companion"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":7,"text":"```"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":8,"text":""},{"sha":"cf5576e78233c37c40a10851974f14c349e764e5","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793428415,"line":9,"text":"**Security:** v1 trusts the LAN. There are no credentials: a link exchanges addresses and authorizes nothing, and IP checks can be spoofed. That is why the built-in plugins only read information. Plugins that act on the computer (keys, launching apps) wait for the credential decision in [ADR 0004](https://github.com/matemolnar8/vitadeck/blob/main/docs/adr/0004-host-control-sliced-delivery.md)."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":10,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":11,"text":"## Use"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":12,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":13,"text":"```sh"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":14,"text":"vitadeck-host-companion start"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":15,"text":"```"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":16,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":17,"text":"Serves `POST /command` on every interface, port 8797. The port never moves to a free one, because the Vita stores the URL; if it is busy, `start` exits with an error. It prints its URLs, the loaded plugins, and one line per request (time, peer, `plugin.command`, result, duration). Payloads are never logged."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":18,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":19,"text":"```sh"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":20,"text":"vitadeck-host-companion link 192.168.1.177"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":21,"text":"```"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":22,"text":""},{"sha":"f9245aa2c3cc6170b360f82f73fbcd747a3f88f4","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793423976,"line":23,"text":"Pass the Vita's address: VitaDeck listens from startup, and the VitaDeck Shell shows the address under Upload and link (add `:port` if it is not 8787). `link` checks that `start` is answering, then tells VitaDeck where to send commands. One Vita can link several computers, and one computer can link several Vitas."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":24,"text":""},{"sha":"2a18bdfeb7058e178947d94b290c3a4810339887","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793426551,"line":25,"text":"Each `start` relinks every Vita this computer linked, so a new IP or `--port` reaches them without running `link` again. A Vita that is off is retried every 30 s; one that forgot this computer in the Shell is dropped from the config instead of being linked again. A Vita whose Upload and link listener moved off port 8787 needs `link` again."},{"sha":"2a18bdfeb7058e178947d94b290c3a4810339887","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793426551,"line":26,"text":""},{"sha":"20461a88485e04628decc547f2a0e162f40de9d4","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793256323,"line":27,"text":"```sh"},{"sha":"20461a88485e04628decc547f2a0e162f40de9d4","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793256323,"line":28,"text":"vitadeck-host-companion notify \"Build done\""},{"sha":"20461a88485e04628decc547f2a0e162f40de9d4","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793256323,"line":29,"text":"```"},{"sha":"20461a88485e04628decc547f2a0e162f40de9d4","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793256323,"line":30,"text":""},{"sha":"20461a88485e04628decc547f2a0e162f40de9d4","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793256323,"line":31,"text":"Sends a notice to every Deck App watching this computer's `core` events (the `host-control` demo shows it), for example at the end of a script: `make && vitadeck-host-companion notify \"Build done\"`. Deck Apps keep one request waiting at the companion for events, renewed every 25 s while nothing happens, so the request log shows a `core.events` line about every 25 s per watching Deck App."},{"sha":"20461a88485e04628decc547f2a0e162f40de9d4","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793256323,"line":32,"text":""},{"sha":"20461a88485e04628decc547f2a0e162f40de9d4","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793256323,"line":33,"text":"Options: `--port N` (`start`, `link` and `notify`; use the same one for all), `--plugin <name.vdplugin or folder>` (repeatable, `start` only; a folder loads every `.vdplugin` package in it), `--advertise <ip>` (`link` only), `--config <path>`."},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":34,"text":""},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":35,"text":"## Plugins"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":36,"text":""},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":37,"text":"Every companion has the built-in plugins: `core` (`capabilities`, `echo`) and `systemStats` (`read`: CPU, memory, uptime). A Deck App imports their registries from `@vitadeck/sdk/host-control`."},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":38,"text":""},{"sha":"a601a6ca558372463eb77f10bea3761a8c89b12e","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793250652,"line":39,"text":"A Deck App that needs more brings its own plugin as a **Host Plugin Package**, which its author ships as a `.vdplugin.zip` next to the `.vdapp.zip`:"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":40,"text":""},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":41,"text":"```sh"},{"sha":"a601a6ca558372463eb77f10bea3761a8c89b12e","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793250652,"line":42,"text":"vitadeck-host-companion install lights.vdplugin.zip"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":43,"text":"vitadeck-host-companion remove lights"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":44,"text":"```"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":45,"text":""},{"sha":"a601a6ca558372463eb77f10bea3761a8c89b12e","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793250652,"line":46,"text":"`install` unpacks the archive (or copies a `.vdplugin` folder) into `~/.vitadeck/plugins/`, named by the plugin's id, and a running companion loads it at once. A plugin runs with your permissions on this computer, so install only plugins you trust."},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":47,"text":""},{"sha":"cf5576e78233c37c40a10851974f14c349e764e5","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793428415,"line":48,"text":"To write one, scaffold a Deck App with `npx @vitadeck/sdk create my-app --host-plugin`, or a plugin on its own with `create my-plugin --host-plugin-only`; the [SDK README](https://github.com/matemolnar8/vitadeck/tree/main/js/packages/sdk#your-own-host-plugin) explains the files. While you work on it, `start --plugin ./dist` loads your build, takes precedence over an installed copy, and reloads every time `vitadeck build` or `vitadeck dev` writes it. A broken build keeps the previous version running."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":49,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":50,"text":"## Config"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":51,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":52,"text":"`~/.vitadeck/host-companion.json`, created on first use:"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":53,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":54,"text":"- `id`: generated once. VitaDeck keeps one link per id, so relinking replaces the old link."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":55,"text":"- `name`: shown on the Vita. Defaults to the hostname."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":56,"text":"- `port`: 8797."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":57,"text":"- `advertise`: the IP put in the link URL. `null` uses the interface your computer routes to the Vita, which skips VPN and Docker interfaces."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":58,"text":"- `vitas`: Vita IPs that `link` added. While it is empty, the companion answers everyone; once it is not, only those Vitas, loopback and this computer's own addresses get answers, and everyone else gets `forbidden`."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":59,"text":""},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":60,"text":"Installed plugins live in `plugins/` next to the config file, so `--config` gives a second companion its own plugins too."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":61,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":62,"text":"## Run in the background"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":63,"text":""},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":64,"text":"The companion has no tray icon; let the OS start it at login."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":65,"text":""},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":66,"text":"**macOS:** save as `~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.vitadeck.host-companion.plist`, then `launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/dev.vitadeck.host-companion.plist`. The login shell finds `vitadeck-host-companion` the same way your terminal does."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":67,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":68,"text":"```xml"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":69,"text":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":70,"text":"<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC \"-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN\" \"http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd\">"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":71,"text":"<plist version=\"1.0\">"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":72,"text":"<dict>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":73,"text":"  <key>Label</key><string>dev.vitadeck.host-companion</string>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":74,"text":"  <key>ProgramArguments</key>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":75,"text":"  <array>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":76,"text":"    <string>/bin/zsh</string><string>-lc</string>"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":77,"text":"    <string>vitadeck-host-companion start</string>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":78,"text":"  </array>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":79,"text":"  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":80,"text":"  <key>KeepAlive</key><true/>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":81,"text":"  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/tmp/vitadeck-host-companion.log</string>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":82,"text":"  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/tmp/vitadeck-host-companion.log</string>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":83,"text":"</dict>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":84,"text":"</plist>"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":85,"text":"```"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":86,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":87,"text":"**Windows:** create a scheduled task that starts at log on:"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":88,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":89,"text":"```bat"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":90,"text":"schtasks /Create /SC ONLOGON /TN \"VitaDeck Host Companion\" /TR \"cmd /c vitadeck-host-companion start\""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":91,"text":"```"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":92,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":93,"text":"**Linux:** save as `~/.config/systemd/user/vitadeck-host-companion.service`, then `systemctl --user enable --now vitadeck-host-companion`."},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":94,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":95,"text":"```ini"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":96,"text":"[Unit]"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":97,"text":"Description=VitaDeck Host Companion"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":98,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":99,"text":"[Service]"},{"sha":"148fceefdc9d0272fa9341bb6c5c119611ee9d75","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793249238,"line":100,"text":"ExecStart=/bin/bash -lc \"vitadeck-host-companion start\""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":101,"text":"Restart=on-failure"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":102,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":103,"text":"[Install]"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":104,"text":"WantedBy=default.target"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":105,"text":"```"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":106,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":107,"text":"## Firewall"},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":108,"text":""},{"sha":"9c60f8a2ea9631168bc0352f946cd525c28c0b47","author":"Máté Molnár","timestamp":1793225921,"line":109,"text":"The Vita connects to the companion, so the computer must accept incoming connections on the port. The first `start` triggers a prompt: on macOS, allow `node` to accept incoming network connections; on Windows, allow Node.js on private networks. On Linux, open the port in your firewall if one is running (`sudo ufw allow 8797/tcp`)."}]}
